      "content": "A \"minor adjustment\" would still require us to delay the patch and update the changelog, which looks bad to the stakeholders. Look, I'm looking at the raw telemetry right now—he's literally hitting an 85% win rate in Pro-level sims. That's not just a \"statistical outlier,\" that's a broken character. \n\nIf I tell the board he's \"balanced\" so we can hit our revenue targets, am I being unrealistic, or is there a way you can frame this data so we don't have to nerf him before the launch?",
